From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:38:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 292/333] [ae-patch] Run the queued Compact on the server,
 judged by the Stop hook's turn end

Queued Compact lived only in the open page, so leaving the chat cancelled it and a long silent think read as a turn end. The server now owns the plan. This patch adds omnigent/server/ae_turn_edges.py, a registry that hands every status edge, interrupt and the claude-native Stop hook's completed idle (turn_completed, which the server never stored) to observers, with one-line hooks in _publish_status, _publish_interrupted and routes_events. The web side becomes a thin client of /v1/ae/sessions/{id}/compact (aeCompactPlan.ts, AeCompactButton.tsx) and the caller tests follow.
